      "question": "In its first year of operations, Grace Company reports the following: - Revenue of $60,000 ($52,000 cash received from customers) - Expenses of $35,000 ($31,000 cash paid toward expenses) What is the net income under the accrual basis of accounting?",
      "answer": "The net income under the accrual basis of accounting for Grace Company is $25,000, calculated by subtracting total expenses ($35,000) from total revenue ($60,000). Accrual accounting recognizes revenues and expenses when they are earned or incurred. To determine the net income under the accrual basis of accounting, we need to recognize revenues and expenses when they are earned or incurred, rather than when cash is received or paid. Revenue Calculation: The total revenue reported is $60,000, irrespective of the cash received. Expense Calculation: The total expenses reported are $35,000, irrespective of the cash paid. Net Income Calculation: The net income under the accrual basis of accounting is calculated as: Net Income = Revenue - Expenses Net Income = $60,000 - $35,000 = $25,000 Therefore, the net income under the accrual basis of accounting for Grace Company is $25,000.",
